        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Ruth Goldstein is dead. You didn't ask. It knew."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "RUTH — GONE. 2 open questions closed unanswered."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "🕯️ Ruth Goldstein is dead — the wild. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "What Ruth kept close goes into the ground with them — keepsakes are buried, never taken from the body."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "\"Ruth's gone.\" Sholpan looks at you for a long moment. \"You're not Ruth.\" No heat in it. Just fact. You'll have to earn this face."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Ella blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "📖 LEARNED: Calming Panic (Level 1). Ground them: 5 things you see, 4 you hear, 3 you touch. Breathe with them. Slow is fast."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "📖 LEARNED: Keeping Morale (Level 1). People need small wins. Celebrate the little things. Despair is the real killer."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "🌟 \"MANTLE TRANSFER DETECTED. ...Oh! New face! Same job! Whole new set of tricks. We hardly noticed. (That is a lie. We noticed. The audience CRIED.)\""
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "📖 The Codex turns a page: Ruth Goldstein, 70 days. The mantle passes to Ella Johnson."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "🪞 You wake up somebody else. Ella Johnson, 67 — an ESL teacher. Her hands know different work now: Green Whisper, Scream Cheese, Green Thumb, Literally."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "You knew Ruth — not the office, the person. The fire keeps expecting her, and so do you. That's a heavier kind of stepping up. (+5 trauma)"
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "At the grave, Sholpan, Boris speak for Ella — \"Ruth trusted them. We saw it. Give them the fire's hearing.\" The village listens."
        },
        {
          "kind": "say",
          "line": "The fire knew Ella before the Codex did — her name already carried weight here."
        }
